title: 'cumulus: judge unincluded blocks by their executing runtime'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    After a V2 -> V3 runtime upgrade, the parent search judged every unincluded block by the best
    block's runtime, which is V3. The V2-executed upgrade block was then kept and resubmitted under
    V3 rules even after its relay parent had expired under V2 rules, and validators rejected the
    candidates.

    The parent search now judges each unincluded block by the runtime that executed it, its
    parent's:

    - V3-executed blocks need a relay parent known from the scheduling parent.
    - V2-executed blocks need a relay parent in the V2 lookahead window. An expired upgrade block
      is therefore dropped and rebuilt instead of resubmitted forever.
    - V2-executed blocks never enter the V3 resubmittable segment.

    After building a runtime upgrade that changes the scheduling version or relay parent offset,
    the slot-based collator stops building new blocks on the slot's later cores; those cores only
    resubmit.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-common
  bump: major
